@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@ to relocate. Two caveats found while reading the call sites:
 - `prepare_replication_entries` also registers `ack_progress` entries, under the
   same `NodeState` write lock, so it inherits that same order.
 
+Directions 1 and 2 were later implemented and measured in
+[ack-state-lock.md](ack-state-lock.md). The ACK path's wait collapsed, but
+throughput did not move. Under `FirstSuccessor` at concurrency 256, owner and
+follower lock waits rose 15-18%. That note also times a second state write lock
+per ACK-waiting write, which this profile never saw.
+
 Direction 2 (cache the topology epoch in an `Arc<AtomicU64>` so the delivery loop
 stops taking a read lock per retry) is consistent with this order and strictly
 removes work; it is worth doing first because it cannot deadlock.
